  "status": "ACTIVE — BETA 0.19 validated aggressive cultural placements + family weights + Aubecourt safety",
  "interpretation": {
    "dino_natural_variant": "For Dino Mounts families, natural wild populations use the matching *_hostile entity. Non-hostile variants remain outside natural spawning and can stay reserved for shops/taming.",
    "weights": "Logical weights and group sizes are read from spawn_profiles_active.json. For terrestrial multi-variant Dino Mounts rules, family_weight is authoritative and is shared across all listed variants by bundle 1.2.23.",
    "night_only": "Barn owl biome placement is active; its pre-existing CubeAnimals spawn-placement predicate is preserved. Strict night-only gating will require a dedicated predicate patch if the original predicate does not enforce darkness.",
    "vanilla_policy": "All natural Overworld spawn lists are cleared in POST_PROCESSING, then explicit Haute Capitale fauna is re-added in the SAME phase, after the clear.",
    "marine_policy": "Strict swimming fauna is handled by aquatic_runtime_rules.json. Thornshell remains amphibious and uses thornshell_behavior_rules.json for bottom-walking/shore-exit behavior.",
    "hmobs_policy": "HMobs is bundled in 1.2.12; its original natural weights/groups are reproduced in the authoritative datapack because the Haute Capitale controller clears/rebuilds Overworld spawn lists.",
    "orc_policy": "General Overworld orcs remain event-only through orc_patrol_rules.json. Natural orc populations are restricted to #capitale_creatures:orc_dungeon and bounded by orc_dungeon_rules.json.",
    "cultural_biomes": "BETA 0.16 narrows terrestrial habitat tags to the validated cultural geography: Empire, Elves, Nordics and Dwarves. Desert/badlands remain the provisional Orc dry territory. Cities and corruption are excluded from ordinary wildlife.",
    "everywhere_surface": "Rules historically described as 'everywhere' now target #capitale_creatures:cultural_surface_land rather than #capitale_creatures:all_overworld. all_overworld stays broad because the controller still needs it for global vanilla/mod spawn clearing.",
    "family_weighting": "A species with several colors/sexes receives one logical spawn budget. Bundle 1.2.23 uses an internal scale of 12 so 2/3/4 variants can share a family weight exactly without changing relative weights of ordinary mobs.",
    "aggressive_pool_pass": "BETA 0.17 only starts aggressive-pool balancing. Passive wildlife is intentionally deferred. Maggot/Baby Spider/Corpse Fly weights/groups are reduced and hostile HMobs are assigned to MONSTER.",
    "validated_aggressive_placements": "BETA 0.19 applies Arthur-approved aggressive/monster placements. Raven is explicitly excluded. Droughtroot Forest Hag is reserved for a future haunted-forest biome and is not naturally spawned yet.",
    "cave_policy": "Cave-only rules currently target vanilla lush_caves and dripstone_caves. A future runtime underground predicate can extend them below surface biomes without polluting surface spawn lists.",
    "marine_myths_policy": "Myths of the Sea natural placement remains staged until aquatic AI validation; bundle 1.2.25 extends generic 3D marine locomotion/water-breathing support to fishlike Myths entities, excluding amphibious Bunyip."
  },
